From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:51:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000: Enable internal storage on the iPod
 touch 6 only

The T7000 ANS nodes enable the ANS1 storage processor on every A8 board
from t7000-common.dtsi, and its mailbox from t7000.dtsi. Only the iPod
touch 6 (N102) has run it: leave both disabled in the SoC files and
enable them in t7000-n102.dts. The firmware region stays described for
every board; m1n1 fills it in from the ADT.

Also keep ps_ans on, as the s5l8960x HACK does for the A7. The boot
loader started the ANS firmware and the ADT marks it no-shutdown: iOS
never powers it down. Without this the domain could go off before the
driver (a module here) binds, once the mailbox suspends or unused
domains are turned off.

The ANS node matches the N102 ADT: ans at 0x208040000 (0x2000 of
registers), interrupts 36-39, and a pre-loaded firmware nub with
segment-ranges for m1n1 to read.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-common.dtsi |  1 -
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts    | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi        |  1 +
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-common.dtsi
index 11f251162..ca6507d2d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-common.dtsi
@@ -45,5 +45,4 @@
 &ans {
 	memory-region = <&ans_firmware>;
 	memory-region-names = "firmware";
-	status = "okay";
 };
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts
index 2c189bd5d..96192afa3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts
@@ -47,6 +47,23 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Internal NAND through the ANS1 storage processor. The
+ * boot loader started its firmware and iOS never shuts it down
+ * (no-shutdown in the ADT), so keep its power domain on, as on the A7.
+ */
+&ans {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ans_mbox {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ps_ans {
+	apple,always-on;
+};
+
 &framebuffer0 {
 	power-domains = <&ps_disp0 &ps_mipi_dsi>;
 };
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi
index 3a93dbe2e..22e529016 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi
@@ -173,6 +173,7 @@
 				"recv-empty", "recv-not-empty";
 			#mbox-cells = <0>;
 			power-domains = <&ps_ans>;
+			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
 		serial0: serial@20a0c0000 {
